  "notes": "Everything that may change when new clips arrive lives here. Times in 'in', 'out' and 'from_source_s' are seconds in the SOURCE file. 'start_s', 'end_s' are seconds from the start of the section picture. Paths are relative to the ayah-lens project root. Set fallback.enabled to true to ship without the s5 placeholder. v1.1 adds the opening fades and title card, the s3b architecture section with the API-references beat, the s6 deep narration and the rubric plates. v1.1b: s6 narration now starts after the API card has left; see the s3b end_at and the s6 gap. v1.2: 0.5 s picture crossfades at every section boundary (timing.crossfade_s), narration starts on the first frame after each fade, new narration files s3-v12, s3b-v12, s6-v12, s7-v12, node 6 and s7 plates reworded, budget savings in s1 / s3b / s7. limits.cap_s is the hard cap; render_v1.py refuses a longer plan unless --allow-over-cap is given (then the file is named -OVER-CAP). v1.2 final: s6-v12 and s7-v12 were regenerated shorter (the stale-decisions sentence left s6, the first two sentences left s7), so s6 shows three lines; the phone clip stays at 24.0 s because its last phrase (22.6-23.6 s) is speech, not silence. v1.3: s7 close reworked so the Hifz and teacher ideas read as future uses (s7-v13 narration, a 'Today' line and a red 'NEXT, WITH MORE DEVELOPMENT' block of three 44 px lines); time budget steps applied: s3b card 4.5 -> 3.5 s, lens segment 5.0 -> 4.0 s, title hold 1.2 -> 0.8 s, s7 tail 1.5 -> 1.0 s.",
